						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-4663/comments/show">SCP-4663</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838511">
									

<p><strong>I am not an official reviewer so take what I say with a grain of salt! This is more of a &quot;what feels wrong with this article and where can it be improved?&quot;</strong><br />
I like the concept, but I feel like it was developed the wrong way/didn't explore everything.</p>
<ul>
<li>Containment doesn't take into account that &quot;SCP-4663 is capable of consuming all inorganic substances&quot;. (<tt>Unanswered Question</tt>)</li>
<li>SCP-4663-1 instances are alive even though they're made from thread that is created from inorganic substances? I don't think this really adds much except as an excuse to not experiment on SCP-4663-1 using 3D-printer-based experiments. (<tt>Doesn't Make Sense + Unanswered Question</tt>)</li>
<li>&quot;physical changes and evolutions happen frequently,&quot; This feels more like an excuse for the Addendum which doesn't really add to the article since it's just random. What of the old SCP-4663 instances? I feel that an experiment/test log would be more appropriate than the Addendum, <em>though that alone might not improve the overall article</em>. (<tt>Doesn't Make Sense + Unanswered Question + Engagement Difficulty</tt>)</li>
<li>Even if you keep the Addendum, it pokes at a <em>&quot;what-if&quot;</em> that's not further explored. Maybe a post-incident report or purposefully recreating the incident in a controlled environment? (<tt>Unanswered Question + Engagement Difficulty</tt>)</li>
</ul>
<p>Currently a 4/10<br />
no vote</p>
