<p>My one comment of substance from a practical standpoint is that this would have to be a massive table. Unbelievably huge. Bloody massive. It might be more workable if this was a table with interchangeable leaves? Perhaps it has multiple leaves for, say, the Atlantic, the Great Lakes, the Med, the North and South Pacific, the Indian Ocean, the Baltic/North Sea/English Channel region? This is just a thought, of course. That would make it less than ideal, because while incredibly useful you couldn't possibly monitor every ship everywhere at once. &quot;We can watch all of the Soviet and Norwegian moves in the Arctic, but we're very concerned about China in the Indian Ocean just now. Both are critical hotpoints. Where do we focus?&quot;</p>

