																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13896672/parasitic-amoeba">Parasitic Amoeba</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838494">
									

<p>1) If you want this to be an end-of-the-world scenario, then the amoebae needs to have a way of spreading and doing so fast. Going after poor people is not the best ticket to do that. Also, there's the question of how it would survive basic purification practices (large containers frequently use tablets every so often in order to keep infectants like bacteria and mold from becoming a problem; amoebae would be included in that due to the danger of dysentery, which is caused by them).</p>
<p>2) The Foundation needs to be included in this somehow. If this is solely something that happens on the periphery and no one has heard of it, then that means that neither has The Foundation and it, therefore, wouldn't be in their catalog.</p>
<p>3) There's also way too much mystery on this. Remember: Less is more. A mysterious stranger that disappears when he dumps something into a container and has the ability to paralyze people is a lot of steps too far here. A mysterious stranger dumping stuff when no one is around and only getting caught as a glimpse in a security camera is a lot more effective (and also gives The Foundation something to put into a case file).</p>
<p>Even if the figure is a humanoid amoeba (which would be a fun twist), it needs to act within the limits of such (such as leaving clothes behind when it de-manifests) in order to be scary. It should maybe also leave behind some sort of mucous.</p>
<p>4) While it's always interesting to see a new disease-based anomaly, this one has a lot of work. You may want to do some research on dysentery (a more rapid form would work well here, especially if it targets specific organs and causes them to shut down far more rapidly than normal).</p>

							</div>

								
					
