<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Unsure, guidance requested</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An 18th century naval war table that displays the location of every military vessel currently on water in the world.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The war table is suspected to have been made during the American Revolution*, leading to many of the naval battles of the war ending in British defeat despite their superiority on sea. It is also thought to have been used in the battles of Manila Bay (1898) and Coronel (1914), as well as many decisive (and unlikely) engagements in WWII. Following the war, the object was considered displaced and eventually lost until resurfacing in the continental US some 50 years later. Through unclear means, it had ended up in an antique shop where its outrageous price had scared off any buyers for years until the Foundation's involvement.</p>
<p>*the nature of the Battle of Quiberon Bay in 1759 has raised concerns regarding the object's assumed creation date.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
