<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The title of this thread: an Enigma dilemma. In WWII, Britain cracked the Enigma cipher. However, using this to save <em>every</em> Allied naval convoy from U-boats would have made it obvious to the Germans that their cipher has been cracked, and so Allied command was faced with a question: you know where, what, and when the enemy will strike. Which attacks do you let happen and which attacks do you thwart?</p>
<p>This SCP is a similar question but on a far larger scale; every public, secret, and clandestine naval movement is laid bare. Any naval force secretly moving against another would force the international, humanity-shielding Foundation to either pick sides, or let conflict after conflict happen. With what could happen if it fell into the wrong hands, and with GOIs interested in acquiring the object, securing, containing, and protecting is very literal.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This would be my first contribution to the site and as such, I would appreciate thorough criticism. There are currently no drafts and I am not counting on this being approved or greenlit, though that would be a nice surprise. Additionally, I'd like some help with the genres—or is History alone enough?</p>
