																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13896448/a-helping-hand-seeking-greenlight">A helping hand (Seeking Greenlight)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838463">
									

<p>1) If it can't be contained and it doesn't appear to be controlled by any stretch, how were they able to test it? Also, if it teleports, why wouldn't the tracker fall off when it teleported? They must have had some incredible reflexes to have tagged it.</p>
<p>2) Setting it at &quot;Keter&quot; may be a little high; I get that it can't be contained, but it's also relatively safe. I could see &quot;Euclid&quot; due to how hard it is to contain, but I'm not sure it's that dangerous.</p>
<p>3) Given that it's just a hand, does it have a limit on how much it can lift? This would affect its usefulness, as well as its ability to wield weapons. Also, how often is it helping?</p>
<p>[Obligatory: I'm seeing parallels between this and the D&amp;D spell &quot;mage hand&quot;, which has a limit of about 5 pounds. While it doesn't need to apply here, it does make for an obvious question.]</p>
<p>4) If the hand is making no pains to remain hidden, how is it avoiding having a presence on social media? Assuming it's helping as often as it can, or even as rarely as once a week, it would develop some sort of following.</p>
<p>5) Overall, it's a great idea and it's nice to see a more positive anomaly. It just needs to be a little more detailed.</p>

							</div>

								
					
